-- title:
--   Igusa's good reduction of X₁(M) in degree form
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Write $F =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC κ M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC κ (Gamma1 M)` of ratios of integral forms of level $\Gamma_1(M)$, that is, `qExpFunctionFieldC κ (Gamma1 M)`. Let $t \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC κ`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\kappa[[q]]$ of the integral power series `jNum` $= E_4^3 \cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv`, so $t$ is the $q$-expansion of $j$ reduced to characteristic $p$. Then $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\kappa\langle t\rangle =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin κ {t}` generated by $t$ inside $F$, with
--   $$[F : \kappa(t)] = [\,\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(M) \sqcup \langle -1\rangle\,],$$
--   the index in $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with the powers of $-1$, i.e. of $\pm\Gamma_1(M)$.
--
--   This is Igusa's good reduction theorem for $X_1(M)$ in the form of an equality of function field degrees: in characteristic $p \nmid M$ the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_1(M)$ has the same degree over $\kappa(j)$ as in characteristic zero, namely the index of $\pm\Gamma_1(M)$. It underlies the later analysis of orders and places on `x1FunctionFieldC`, including the computation of the order of $t$ minus a constant and the bound on the index of $\Gamma_1(M)$ in terms of the supersingular locus.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrank_adjoin_x1FunctionFieldC_eq_index_gamma1_sup_of_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib
